Description: A user-friendly Shiny application for genomic variant analysis
    with two main modules. The Marker Selection module evaluates VCF files 
    against marker panel information, visualizing marker distribution across 
    the genome with filtering options for minor allele frequency (MAF), read 
    depth, missing data, repeated regions, and copy number differences from 
    expected ploidy. The CNV Profiles module enables interactive visualization 
    of copy number variation patterns by sample or family, with integrated 
    B-allele frequency (BAF) and z-score profile plots for comprehensive 
    chromosomal aberration assessment.
